@theme homesick
// Writer-commons, themes batch. From content/arcs/outlines.md, "The struggle themes". Any department, either shift.
// Fill-ins assumed: {home} a place ("Lisk"), {family} with "my" ("my gran"), {hobby} an activity ("painting"),
// {since} a length of time ("five years"). A beat that names one lists it in needs:, so people without it skip it.

== beat 1
tone: light
needs: home
hint: Funny thing. I smelt bread in the mess and I was somewhere else entirely.
mem: smell
them: Funny. Smelt bread in the mess this morning and I was back on {home}. Just for a second.
them: It rains there, mostly. You'd think I'd be glad to be dry.   [laugh]
? choice
* What's it like, {home}?   flavour:listen mem:asked
  them: Small. Wet. Loud markets. You'd hate it. You'd love it.
  + them: Small and wet and loud, and everyone knows your business. Sit down. I'll tell you properly.
* Dry's overrated.   flavour:cheer
  them: Says someone who's never been rained on for a week straight. Lucky you.   [laugh]
them: Anyway. Bread. That's all. Just bread.

== beat 2
tone: heartfelt
needs: home
hint: Got a minute? I'm meant to be calling home. I keep not doing it.
mem: call
them: I've walked to the booths three times today. Walked back three times.   [sigh]
them: It's not that anything's wrong. It's that everything's fine, and I'm not there for it.
them: I miss {home}. There. I've said it. I don't say it, normally.
? choice
* I'll walk to the booths with you. I'll wait outside.   flavour:practical mem:walked
  them: Would you? Yes. Then I can't walk back. Not with you watching.
  + them: Yes. Please. You're good at this, you know. Making things smaller.
* What do you miss most?   flavour:listen mem:most
  them: The noise. Here it hums. At home it chatters. I didn't know I'd miss chattering.
* I miss home too, some days.   flavour:share mem:shared
  them: Yeah? Good. I mean, not good. But good I'm not the only one.
them: Right. Booths. Before I change my mind.

== beat 3
tone: resolution
needs: home
hint: Come and eat with me. Something happened. A good something.
mem: dish
them: Look at this. Brennan made it. A dish from {home}. I never asked. Somebody told her.   [laugh]
them: And I called home last night. It went fine. Better than fine. They all talked at once.
them: It's still far. It's just not as far as it was.
? choice
* I may have mentioned it to Brennan.   flavour:practical mem:brennan
  them: You didn't. You did! You're a menace. Thank you.
* Tastes like home?   flavour:listen
  them: Nearly. Brennan says nearly is the best anyone gets. She's right. It's lovely.
  + them: Nearly. Close enough to close my eyes. Here, have a spoonful. This is where I'm from.
them: Same table tomorrow? I'll tell you about the rain.
